course: dictionary
lesson: 13565
title: Inadvertently
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Inadvertently is an adverb. It tells you how something happened: by accident, without meaning to. «She inadvertently knocked over the vase while reaching for her bag.» Nobody wanted the vase to fall, so inadvertently tells you it was an accident.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. Did the person plan it or want it? If not, inadvertently may be the right word. «He inadvertently deleted his homework, so he had to write it again.» He did not mean to delete it, and the rest of the sentence shows that.
explain: Be careful: inadvertently is the opposite of on purpose. «She deliberately hid the cake» means she meant to hide it. To check your meaning, swap in "by accident". If the sentence still makes sense, you have understood the word.
fact: Inadvertently means by accident, without meaning to.
fact: Inadvertently is an adverb, so it tells you how an action happened.
fact: You can inadvertently hurt someone's feelings or share a secret, without wanting to.
fact: Online, you can inadvertently share your location in a photo, so check pictures before you post them.
fact: In 1928 Alexander Fleming made a discovery inadvertently: he found penicillin by chance, not by planning it.
exercise: «He inadvertently left his bag on the bus.» What does inadvertently mean here? | Again and again | *By accident, without meaning to | Very quickly and loudly | On purpose, as a joke
exercise: «Sam inadvertently deleted the photo.» Did Sam mean to delete it? | He did it twice, on purpose | Yes, he did it on purpose | *No, it happened by accident | Yes, because he was angry with it
exercise: Which phrase could replace inadvertently in «She inadvertently spilled the juice»? | on purpose | very slowly | *by accident | with a big smile
test: «The message was inadvertently sent to the wrong person.» What does inadvertently suggest? | It was sent very loudly | *It was sent by accident | It was never sent at all | It was sent on purpose to a friend
test: Mia says inadvertently means very angrily. Is she right? | Yes, it means sadly | Yes, it means very angrily | No, it means very quickly | *No, it means by accident, without meaning to
exam: What does inadvertently mean in «I inadvertently stepped on the cat's tail»? | Very carefully | *By accident | Slowly and sadly | On purpose, to tease the cat
